From 80392a0107dbbcaee5aa3d6a2550b355ba95dc1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:55:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] minigbm: never hold DRM master

Opening a PRIMARY node makes the opener master whenever the device has no
master yet (drm_master_open()), and gralloc starts early enough to win that
race. Once the dumb backend started declining render nodes and falling through
to card nodes, that is exactly what happened: the allocator took master and
drm_hwcomposer could not,

    drmSetMaster(*GetFd());
    if (drmIsMaster(*GetFd()) == 0) {
            ALOGE("DRM/KMS master access required");     DrmDevice.cpp:116-119

so it fell back to a headless null-display -- a console with no GUI, on a
machine whose display was working one commit earlier.

Only the compositor should be master. The allocator needs the card node purely
for DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, which is declared with no flags
(drm_ioctl.c:708) and therefore does not require master at all.

Dropping it right after open is harmless on render nodes and whenever we did
not become master -- it just returns an error, which is why the result is
ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qqqf5AZFdnmaLmddmG16pW
Change-Id: I4fe491b18c5d96be064181841ac7ed27364271cd
---
 cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
index 706dee9..389fb5f 100644
--- a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
+++ b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
@@ -109,6 +109,27 @@ static struct driver *init_try_node(int idx, char const *str)
 	if (fd < 0)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * Never hold DRM master.
+	 *
+	 * Opening a PRIMARY node makes the opener master whenever the device has
+	 * no master yet (drm_master_open()), and gralloc is started early enough
+	 * to win that race. drm_hwcomposer then cannot get it:
+	 *
+	 *     drmSetMaster(*GetFd());
+	 *     if (drmIsMaster(*GetFd()) == 0) {
+	 *             ALOGE("DRM/KMS master access required");   DrmDevice.cpp:116-119
+	 *
+	 * and it falls back to a headless null-display -- a console with no GUI.
+	 * Only the compositor should be master; the allocator needs the node for
+	 * DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, which carries no flags (drm_ioctl.c:708) and
+	 * so does not require it.
+	 *
+	 * Harmless on render nodes and whenever we did not become master: it
+	 * simply returns an error, which is why the result is ignored.
+	 */
+	drmDropMaster(fd);
+
 	drv = drv_create(fd, NULL);
 	if (!drv)
 		close(fd);
